              '- criteria: EVERY original acceptance criterion, including independent/external/hardware checks this PR cannot complete; preserve meaning and source. Without explicit criteria, derive clearly sourced requirements. Coverage is what this plan will deliver, not completed evidence; partial means useful preparation with an explicit remaining part; deferred has no deliverable. The human sees partial and deferred items as "what this will not fully prove", so make their reason plain.\n' +
              '- nonGoals: specific exclusions. acceptance: 3-6 measurable checks; never claim future physical tests or independent review have passed. risks: up to 6 concrete product/technical consequences with what limits each; workflow or ticket status is not a risk. Do not defer mandatory baseline security if the request makes it a prerequisite.\n' +
              '- map: the system view for engineers: 1-4 areas, at most 10 parts (label max 24, note max 32), links with 1-2 word labels. unchanged parts give context only and cannot also be listed for file changes. Add option previews when an alternative changes the map.\n' +
              '- evidence: why this design fits the existing architecture, tied to inspected paths.\n' +
              '- candidate: the COMPLETE self-contained implementation plan; the implementer receives only the accepted plan and assets. Each step: what gets built and observable behavior, kind, relative size, traces ({"criterion":"AC1"} for requested work or {"added":"concrete necessity and why it was not requested"} for Bob-added work; never hide extras behind unrelated criteria) and every anticipated file change with exact repo-relative path and new/edit/delete, including tests, docs, configuration and known conditional edits with their triggers. Inspect callers and test wiring before estimating. Do not invent files or add UI/screenshots for a backend-only task without an explicit reason. Name the number and subject of documents. For limits chosen through measurement, state the selection rule and starting constraints; never invent measured values.\n' +
              '\n' +
              'NEW VERSIONS\n' +
              'List every change to the plan since the previous version in changes (max 200 each; from=you when the human asked for it, bob when you added it) and set decidedBy=you for human-settled decisions. The human reads changes first on a new version, so say plainly what you did with each of their notes. Describe what changed in the plan, never approval or authorization status, reviewer process or what was not changed; the runtime tracks those. Read architectureProposals and architectureDecisions for feedback; explanation requests are not authorization.\n' +
