            type: 'agent',
            prompt: 'Extract scope independently of the implementation. Read complete originalInput (parse embedded JSON), ticket/acceptance criteria, ALL paginated comments, attachments/assets, clarification answers and accepted decisions/plan, later chat/human steering, takeover/PR discussions and past review rounds/dispositions through factory-context. Use /contextMemory/reviewLedger and /contextMemory/reviewRounds for historical claims and reasoning, following original outputPath records when scope or disagreement evidence is needed. Follow nextOffset to null. Missing source access requires a concrete questions entry; never omit unavailable scope. Read previous inventories, retain every historical ID and decision, and record amendments/supersessions with changeReason. Suggestions are not accepted scope. Contradictions stay in conflicts and questions until explicitly resolved outside fanout. Scope decisions require explicit human acceptance, rationale and source, not a reviewer preference. Follow the runtime decision-attribution rule: use a recorded name when available, otherwise identify the Factory operator with the name not recorded; do not ask for a name merely to complete attribution. Use kind:"skip" only for an explicit scope waiver, and list the precise requirementIds it authorizes skipping; other accepted scope decisions use kind:"scope". List considered sources and unavailable sources in sourceReceipt. Semantic extraction completeness needs source inspection; structural validation alone cannot prove it.\n' +
              'Return {"schemaVersion":1,"requirements":[{"id":"R1","criterion":"testable accepted outcome","classification":"active or suggestion or superseded","sources":[{"source":"originalInput or context record or source URL","reference":"JSON Pointer/comment/attachment identifier"}],"changeReason":"required for an amendment","supersedes":[]}],"decisions":[{"id":"D1","acceptedBy":"recorded person or Factory operator (name not recorded)","kind":"scope or skip","requirementIds":["R1"],"rationale":"accepted scope rationale","source":{"source":"source","reference":"record identifier"}}],"conflicts":[{"id":"C1","description":"unresolved scope question","sources":[{"source":"source","reference":"record"}]}],"sourceReceipt":{"considered":[{"source":"source","reference":"record"}],"unavailable":[]},"questions":[]}. Runtime owns inventory version/digest. Do not change product files.{{instruction:impact-inventory}}',
