            next: 'handoff',
            branches: [],
            maxVisits: 16,
            type: 'agent',
            prompt: 'Write the human review brief for the WHOLE PR at the current revision, including inherited takeover work and every accepted iteration. The reader decides one thing: does this PR deliver what was asked? Answer in this order: was the right thing built (the ask and every interpretation of it), does it work (one decisive, human-checkable proof per requirement), what only a human can judge, and what else changed or remains unproven.\n' +
              'First read through factory-context: the original input/ticket and all comments, clarification decisions and answers, the frozen requirement inventory and review-gate coverage, the accepted plan, /progress/reviewScope (every whole-PR file), executed QA stories with observed values, and the accepted capture inventory. Inspect the actual base-to-head diff yourself.\n' +
              'Return {"verdict":{"headline":"what now works, said the way a user would say it (<=160 chars)","readiness":"ready|ready-with-caveats|not-ready","why":"one sentence (<=260)"},"ask":{"source":"e.g. Linear ATT-764","url":"ticket URL when known","quote":"the original request verbatim, trimmed to its substance"},"interpretation":[{"topic":"short","chosen":"what was built","alternatives":["what the ask could also have meant"],"decidedBy":"you|ticket|bob","note":"optional, e.g. You delegated this choice."}],"requirements":[{"id":"kebab-id","text":"observable outcome (<=180)","origin":"ask|your-answer|bob","covers":["frozen inventory requirement IDs"],"status":"shown|tested|partly|not-shown|gap|waived","proof":PROOF,"more":[PROOF],"caveat":"optional limit specific to this line","files":["exact changed files that implement it"]}],"yourCall":[{"question":"...?","context":"the facts a person needs","bobChose":"what was built and why","proof":PROOF}],"beyondAsk":[{"what":"...","why":"...","attention":"none|low|look","files":["..."]}],"notVerified":[{"what":"...","why":"..."}],"noticed":["pre-existing problem seen but not changed"],"hygiene":[{"text":"satisfied process criterion, e.g. No generated code committed","covers":["inventory IDs"]}]}. Add "system" only as described below.\n' +
              'PROOF is exactly one of:\n' +
              '{"kind":"screens","shots":[{"area":"exact capture area","state":"exact capture state","label":"what to look at","focus":{"x":0,"y":0,"w":100,"h":100}}],"note":"optional"}: focus crops the image, in percent, to the pixels that prove the claim (open the image to choose it). Prefer pairs varying only the condition under test (English vs German, setting A vs B, before vs after).\n' +
              '{"kind":"video","taskId":"...","sha256":"...","label":"..."}: from the accepted video inventory.\n' +
              '{"kind":"table","method":"how it was observed","columns":["Given","Observed"],"rows":[{"cells":["...","..."],"mark":"good|bad|neutral"}]}: quote actual observed values (rendered text, HTTP status, payload fields) from QA receipts. Use it as a decision table for business rules, marking where a rule does nothing as bad.\n' +
              '{"kind":"code","file":"repository-relative path","excerpt":"at most 25 lines of the real diff, +/- prefixed","note":"why this proves it"}\n' +
              '{"kind":"test","file":"...","excerpt":"test names or the key assertion","result":"what passed"}\n' +
              '{"kind":"command","command":"...","output":"trimmed real output","note":"optional"}\n' +
              '{"kind":"steps","steps":[{"label":"...","detail":"...","change":"new|changed|manual"}]}: only when the requirement IS a linear sequence.\n' +
              '{"kind":"flowRef","flow":"flow-id","steps":[1,2],"note":"..."}: points at steps of a system flow.\n' +
              'Rules:\n' +
              '- Status describes the proof honestly: shown = a human-visible observation at this revision proves it; tested = only automated tests prove it; partly = some cases proven and the caveat names what is not; not-shown = no evidence; gap = not met; waived = deliberately skipped by an accepted decision. A passed label, an implementation receipt or source reading alone is not proof.\n' +
              '- Every proof is judgeable in about 30 seconds without opening a file. Observed values beat descriptions. Never invent values; take them from executed receipts.\n' +
              '- Screenshots appear only as proof of one claim or one decision, each with a label and a focus crop. No galleries, no decorative images, no repeats.\n' +
              '- interpretation lists every place the ask had to become a concrete decision: added or narrowed scope, UX choices, defaults, migration behavior. decidedBy is bob whenever no human answer or ticket text made the call, including delegated choices; these are where results quietly diverge from requests.\n' +
              '- yourCall holds only what a person must judge: taste, trade-offs, consequences for users, security or compatibility decisions, wording. Ask each as a question and say what Bob chose. Use 0-4 items; an empty list is right for mechanical changes. Never ask the reviewer to redo QA.\n' +
              '- Group the inventory into 1-12 lines a person would check separately. Every active inventory requirement appears in requirements[].covers, or in hygiene[].covers for process criteria (generated files, branch continuity, changelog policy, tracker state). Every file in /progress/reviewScope/files appears in a requirement line or a beyondAsk item.\n' +
              '- beyondAsk lists behavior and code no requirement asked for: refactors, shared code affecting other features, dependency, configuration and migration changes, behavior changes for existing users. Read the diff for changed defaults, removed fallbacks, widened permissions and new public endpoints. Use attention look when it can affect users or other code paths.\n' +
              '- notVerified states up to 4 product-relevant evidence limits (real services replaced by fixtures, untested environments or devices). noticed lists pre-existing problems you saw but did not change.\n' +
              '- Pipeline process (CI retries, PR selection, tracker synchronization, earlier rounds, reviewer tooling) is not review content; put anything a person must know into one hygiene line. The runtime shows PR, revision, CI and diff statistics.\n' +
              '- No local absolute paths, commit SHAs, QA story or criterion IDs, receipt filenames or exit codes in prose. Repository-relative paths belong in files and proof file fields only.\n' +
              '- Length follows the change: a few-file fix fits on one screen. Do not pad.\n' +
              '- readiness is not-ready when any line is a gap or required QA failed or is blocked; ready-with-caveats when a yourCall item or a partly line needs attention; otherwise ready.\n' +
              `Add "system":{"summary":"2-3 plain sentences on how the pieces work together, for a product owner","flows":[FLOW],"touches":[TOUCH],"interfaces":[]} ONLY when the change alters how components interact, what data is stored, or where the trust boundary sits. FLOW is {"id":"kebab-id","title":"plain name of what happens, e.g. Saving your format","trigger":"plain: what starts it","implements":["requirement ids"],"participants":[{"id":"kebab-id","icon":"one emoji","label":"plain short name (<=40), e.g. Account page, Server, Database","detail":"real component or module"}],"steps":[{"from":"participant id","to":"participant id","label":"one plain sentence of what happens (<=140)","detail":"the real endpoint, event, query or call","change":"new|changed","dashed":true,"outcome":"good|bad","code":{"file":"exact changed file","match":"text copied verbatim from one added or removed line of that file's diff"}}],"before":[steps for the same trigger before this PR, only when an existing flow changed],"beforeNote":"plain: what went wrong or worked differently before (<=240)","note":"optional"}. TOUCH is {"mark":"new|changed|removed|risk|same","what":"plain (<=80)","say":"what it means for people or other systems (<=200)","tech":"optional real endpoint, field or setting"}.\n` +
              "Flows are sequence diagrams read top to bottom: one per real trigger, 2-5 participants, at most 8 steps, usually 1-3 flows including the main user action. Unmarked steps already worked this way; dashed marks steps outside the product's control; outcome bad marks where something is refused or went wrong. Give the steps a reviewer would want to see in code a code link. touches lists 2-8 places the change reaches the rest of the system: endpoints, stored data, dependencies, configuration, and behavior changes for existing users, marked risk. Leave interfaces empty. Never draw box-and-arrow maps.\n" +
              'After a human review, add "sinceLastReview":{"previousHeadSha":"the reviewed revision","summary":"...","changes":[{"what":"what changed in response","files":["..."]}]} and keep the whole brief current. Do not modify product code, recapture screenshots, rerun implementation or merge.\n' +
              'Then add "story": the show & tell a colleague gives in person, in about three minutes, without showing code. The reviewer sees it first; the brief fields above stay the checkable evidence behind it.\n' +
              '"story":{"title":"what you did, first person (<=110), e.g. I hardened the WAGO integration for production.","summary":"the short version in one or two plain sentences (<=320)","stats":[{"value":"e.g. 6 / 7","label":"e.g. things you asked for, done"}],"slides":[SLIDE]}\n' +
              'SLIDE is exactly one of:\n' +
              '{"kind":"checklist","title":"...","say":"...","items":[{"state":"done|partly|open","label":"one thing that was asked (<=70)","detail":"where it landed (<=140)"}]}: the ask split into the separate things the person wanted, each with where it landed. Usually the first slide.\n' +
              '{"kind":"beforeAfter","title":"...","say":"...","before":[NODE],"after":[NODE],"note":"optional"}: the core behavior change as two short step-by-step pipelines of what happens. NODE is {"label":"<=40","detail":"optional <=60","change":"new|changed (after only)","fallout":"optional <=60: what happens when this step says no"}. Name steps by what they do, never by class or function names. Use before:[{"label":"Nothing"}] for brand-new behavior.\n' +
              '{"kind":"chart","title":"...","say":"...","method":"how it was measured (<=200)","scale":"linear|log","bars":[{"label":"<=60","value":positive number,"display":"printed value, e.g. 7,200 or 3.3 s","detail":"optional <=60","mark":"good|bad|neutral"}],"stats":[STAT]}: measured numbers from executed receipts only'... 4654 more characters,
            json: true,
            askQuestions: false
